title: Expansion Plan Item-by-Item Audit — Complete Review
summary: Completed item-by-item audit of all 9 expansion plan initiatives from the competitive landscape analysis. 2 items struck (already shipped as paradigm sync), 2 deferred (external MCP integration needs refinement, dashboard folded into Sentinel Product), 5 active initiatives reviewed and expanded. Created capabilities-inventory.md to prevent proposing existing features. Created sentinel-product-plan.md as separate commercial product document.
symbols_touched:
  - '#paradigm-sync'
  - '#paradigm-doctor'
  - '#paradigm-sweep'
  - '#paradigm-heat-map'
  - '#paradigm-pipeline'
files_created:
  - docs/private/capabilities-inventory.md
  - docs/private/sentinel-product-plan.md
files_modified:
  - docs/private/expansion-plan-2026-q2.md
decisions:
  - id: D-strike-1.1-2.1
    decision: Strike items 1.1 (AGENTS.md export) and 2.1 (cross-tool config export) from plan
    rationale: Both already fully shipped as paradigm sync IDE adapters. Created capabilities-inventory.md to prevent this class of oversight.
  - id: D-defer-2.4
    decision: Defer item 2.4 (external MCP integration) until demand materializes
    rationale: Good idea but needs refinement. No immediate user demand. Revisit later.
  - id: D-defer-3.1
    decision: Fold item 3.1 (governance dashboard) into separate Sentinel Product plan
    rationale: Dashboard is a commercial product concern, not a free CLI feature. Created sentinel-product-plan.md with 4 product tiers.
  - id: D-sweep-fix-default
    decision: Make sweep --fix the default behavior with strict thresholds (14 days staleness, 90% coverage)
    rationale: Anything that runs via CLI at no cost is a must. Be as stringent and forthcoming as possible by default.
  - id: D-heat-map-adaptive
    decision: Expand 2.3 with adaptive heat map where agents detect and maintain query-symbol relevance
    rationale: 3-layer detection (automatic breadcrumbs, explicit agent recording, agent corrections) creates a flywheel where agents are both consumers and maintainers of relevance knowledge.
  - id: D-pipeline-gates
    decision: Make pipeline gates configurable with 3 modes (auto/manual/sentinel) at 3 levels
    rationale: User wants governance decided beforehand per feature type, not blocking on every step. Agents need reasoning to select appropriate governance.
  - id: D-pipeline-mcp
    decision: Add 7 MCP tools for pipeline management so agents have full autonomy
    rationale: Agents need proper tools to manage pipelines — start, advance, configure, escalate, abort, resume, status.
  - id: D-governance-spec-10
    decision: Expand governance spec outline from 8 to 10 items (add Adaptive Context and Development Pipeline)
    rationale: Heat map and pipeline are core governance capabilities that belong in the public spec.
learnings:
  - Always check capabilities-inventory.md before proposing new features to avoid re-proposing shipped work
  - 'CLI-at-no-cost philosophy: anything that can run locally for free is a 100% must'
  - Default to maximum stringency — users can relax, but starting lenient means drift
  - Configurable gate modes (auto/manual/sentinel) resolve the tension between automation and human oversight
  - Agents should have enough reasoning to select governance levels OR know to ask — never be passive executors
  - Separate commercial product planning (Sentinel) from open-source expansion to keep concerns clean
  - The governance spec for public publication should include ALL pillars including new ones (heat map, pipeline)
tags:
  - arc:cross-study
  - arc:expansion-plan
  - strategic
  - review
  - competitive-analysis
body: |-
  ## Full Audit Summary

  ### Items Struck (Already Shipped)
  - **1.1 AGENTS.md Export** — `paradigm sync agents-md` already generates this
  - **2.1 Cross-Tool Config Export** — `paradigm sync` has 5 adapters (Claude, Cursor, Copilot, Windsurf, AGENTS.md)

  ### Items Reviewed and Approved
  - **1.2 Doctor Context Audit** — adds context quality scoring to existing doctor command
  - **1.3 Auto-Graph on Scan** — always re-indexes graph during scan, 2-hour effort

  ### Items Reviewed and Expanded
  - **2.2 Garbage Collection Sweeps** — expanded with --fix as default, 9 entropy checks, strict thresholds (14 days/90%), annotative auto-fixes, automatic lore recording
  - **2.3 Tiered Context + Adaptive Heat Map** — massively expanded with 3-layer adaptive heat map (automatic breadcrumbs, explicit recording, agent corrections), 4 MCP tools, decay/boost mechanics, query-symbol relevance learning
  - **3.2 Spec Pipeline** — expanded with configurable gate modes (auto/manual/sentinel), 3 config levels (project defaults, pipeline templates, per-pipeline override), 7 MCP tools, agent reasoning for template selection, mid-flight adjustment, escalation protocol
  - **3.3 Universal Governance** — spec outline expanded from 8 to 10 items (added Adaptive Context and Development Pipeline)

  ### Items Deferred
  - **2.4 External MCP Integration** — needs refinement, no immediate demand
  - **3.1 Governance Dashboard** — folded into Sentinel Product plan (separate document)

  ### New Documents Created
  - `docs/private/capabilities-inventory.md` — 25 capability domains, 95 MCP tools, 24+ CLI commands
  - `docs/private/sentinel-product-plan.md` — 4 tiers (Team Dashboard, Alerting & CI, Team Analytics, Enterprise)

  ### Active Release Cadence (5 releases)
  v3.25.0 → Personas P5 + auto-graph (1.3)
  v3.26.0 → Doctor context audit (1.2)
  v3.27.0 → Sweep (2.2)
  v3.28.0 → Heat map (2.3)
  v3.29.0 → Pipeline (3.2)
